    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "BUSINESS\nCLASS\nAvocado - an original Pacific Rim tropical fruit.\nNative to South America, the avocado was first discovered by European chefs in the middle of the\nnineteenth century. Now exported to the world by California, New Zealand and South Africa, it's a\nnew classic in modern sushi, and is an old favourite being given a new twist by today's chefs in\nsalads, omelettes and pasta dishes to name a few.\nOur meal service offers you contemporary, brasserie-style cuisine alongside award winning Australasian wines\nTony Adcock, from New Zealand's famous Harbourside Restaurant, helps to define the experience onboard.\nHe works with our team of dedicated chefs and consulting restaurants from around the world to develop\nPacific Rim inspired regional cuisine.\ndInner TOKYO TO AUCKLAND / CHRISTCHURCH\nappetiser\nSushi selection\nwith pickled ginger.\nmain course\nRatatouille crusted lamb\nwith parsley potatoes and\nseasonal vegetables.\nSupreme of cajun chicken\nwith garlic cream sauce,\nsaffron rice, broccoli floret\nand sweet bell peppers.\nTraditional Japanese dish\nof sake steamed sea bream\ntopped with crab meat, served\nwith Japanese vegetables\nand fish sauce.\nMiso soup and Japanese pickles\nto complement your meal.\ndessert\nAlmond nut gateau\nwith vanilla sauce.\nMilk tea and chocolate\nice cream selection.\ncheese and fruit\nA selection of fine cheese\nand seasonal fruit.\nbeverages\nFreshly brewed or\ndecaffeinated coffee, tea\nherbal tea and hot chocolate.\nArtificial sweetener is available.\nLight Choice - an easily\ndigestible, lower fat alternative.\nSNACK\nA selection of sandwiches and\nsnacks are available at any time\nthroughout the flight.\nCUISINE\nA quick meal consisting of a selection\nof breads, the appetiser of the day,\ncheese and chocolates."
    ],
